{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And the sense of <b>standing over him</b> is that they were standing opposite him, looking at him, in the manner of 'the one standing over the reapers' (Ruth 2:5), 'the officers of those standing' (I Kings 5:30). And since he was sitting and they were standing and looking at him, Scripture says 'over him.' And this is the sense of 'and he saw and ran toward them' — for when he saw them standing opposite him and not proceeding on their way, he ran toward them to bring them to his house. And the sense of 'from the entrance of the tent' is to indicate that he was still sitting there after the appearance of the Shekhinah had withdrawn from him. And it is possible that 'over him' refers to the tent — that they were near it on the other side, not opposite the entrance, and they were standing there without drawing near to Abraham, in the sense of 'encamping by the sea' (Exodus 14:9)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:40.682676580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}